# Goal + Flow CODING agent (drives = REAL tools). Each Goal attempt runs a Flow that
# GENERATES a dataflow DAG of CLAUDE CODE agents -- each node has the full file/shell
# toolset -- and Goal's checker (also Claude Code) VERIFIES the acceptance condition by
# ACTUALLY running it, re-attempting until met. This is "verified coding via Goal+Flow"
# that genuinely writes + runs code.
#
# Contrast the LOCAL ollama Goal+Flow: its nodes call jet_backend::run_ollama (a bare LLM
# call, NO tools) -- they can only SIMULATE coding. Real local coding would need the shape
# layer to thread tools/MCP into node calls (a bigger change); `drives:` gets it for free.
#
# SLOW: many Claude Code calls per round. Needs claude-code-acp.
#   jet acp-serve acp_goal_flow_coder_demo::VerifiedCoder::handle examples/acp_goal_flow_coder_demo.jet
# Try: "Create fib.py with fib(n) (0-indexed) and confirm fib(10) == 55 by running it."
module acp_goal_flow_coder_demo
  agent VerifiedCoder
    runner Goal(accept: "the requested code is written to a file AND a SHOWN real command run confirms it works -- the expected output must appear in actual terminal output, not a described or simulated result",
                via: {name: :Flow},
                surface: true,
                max_rounds: 3,
                drives: "claude-code-acp")
    expose handle(task)
  end
end
